<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yang Ganzhen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 928–<a href="/years/937">937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yang Ganzhen was a powerful official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-erhai">Erhai</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>, in the former lands of Nanzhao. In 928 he overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-longdan">Zheng Longdan</a>, last ruler of the Da Changhe, and placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-shanzheng">Zhao Shanzheng</a> on the throne of the short-lived Da Tianxing, before taking power himself and founding the Da <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yining">Yining</a>. He was overthrown in 937 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duan-siping">Duan Siping</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dali-kingdom">Dali Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
